==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:Great Seal of the United States (reverse).svg|thumb|The Latin phrase ''novus ordo seclorum'', appearing on the reverse side of the Great Seal of the United States. Conspiracy theorists claim this is an allusion to the New World Order.]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|new world order}}
* {{alt|en|NWO|q=conspiracy theory}}

===Etymology===
Popularized by {{w|H. G. Wells}} in ''{{w|The New World Order (Wells book)|The New World Order}}'' (1940).

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun|head=[[new|New]] [[world order|World Order]]}}

# A [[vision]] for the world in which greater [[peace]] and [[stability]] is achieved through a new [[political]] order.
#* {{quote-web|en|date=July 18 2012|author=Scott Tobias|work=AV Club|title=The Dark Knight Rises|url=http://www.avclub.com/articles/the-dark-knight-rises-review-batman,82624/|passage=Where the Joker preys on our fears of random, irrational acts of terror, Bane has an all-consuming, dictatorial agenda that’s more stable and permanent, a '''New World Order''' that’s been planned out with the precision of a military coup.}}
# According to [[conspiracy theory|conspiracy theories]], the planned rule of the world by a secret global [[elite]].
#: {{syn|en|NWO}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=08 May 92|journal=Gay Community News|page=3|author=John Zeh|text=She [Urvashi Vaid] also called Supreme Court justices "unqualified, sexist henchmen of the '''new world order'''.}}

